# GEHC Youth Portal — Cursor Rules

## Tech Stack
- Frontend: Vite + React + TypeScript
- Backend: Express.js (ESM .mjs) + Prisma ORM
- Database: TiDB Cloud (MySQL-compatible, serverless)
- AI: Vercel AI SDK (OpenAI gpt-4o-mini + Groq fallback)
- Auth: Google SSO + session cookies (JWT)

## CRITICAL: TiDB Cloud Quirks
- TiDB Cloud Serverless DROPS TCP connections after ~2-5 sequential queries
- NEVER use sequential Prisma/user.update() in for-loops — it WILL hang
- ALWAYS use single CASE WHEN UPDATE for bulk operations (1 SQL statement)
- Prisma ESM import hangs — use CJS (.cjs) for standalone scripts
- Prisma JSON null filter broken — use raw SQL: `WHERE gifts_top5 IS NULL`
- Connection pool exhaustion after ~80 sequential operations

## Project Structure
- `server/index.mjs` — All API endpoints (~4350 lines, DO NOT split)
- `server/auth.mjs` — Auth (Google SSO, local login, session cookies)
- `server/engine.mjs` — Placement algorithm
- `server/jethro-ai.mjs` — AI analysis
- `src/components/portal/` — React components (flat imports, no lazy loading)
- `prisma/schema.prisma` — Database schema

## Conventions
- API endpoints use `wrap(async (req, res) => {...})` pattern
- Auth check: `if (!req.authUser) return res.status(401).json({...})`
- Role check: `requireRole('SUPERADMIN', 'KOMISI')` middleware
- Admin endpoints: manual `req.authUser` check (no middleware)
- Frontend: TypeScript, no comments unless asked, concise

